---
/**
 * The stakes: why tradesmen need a guild (StoryBrand "stakes"). Condensed from
 * the Case for Support. The hardship story is kept to one sentence, without
 * figures, until both members have given written consent.
 */
import Section from '@/components/ui/Section.astro';

const facts = [
  {
    term: 'Dangerous Work',
    text: 'Construction and extraction has the second-highest rate of fatal workplace injury in the nation, nearly four times the average across all occupations.',
  },
  {
    term: 'Lonely Work',
    text: 'Long days alone in a van or on a job site. Research points to isolation and a lack of support as serious concerns across the trades.',
  },
  {
    term: 'No Safety Net',
    text: 'Most Guild members have no employer-sponsored health insurance. Some have no coverage at all.',
  },
];
---

<Section tone="paper" labelledby="need-title">
  <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[3fr_2fr] lg:gap-16">
    <div>
      <h2 id="need-title" class="text-h2">
        Why Tradesmen Need a Guild
      </h2>
      <div class="mt-5 flex max-w-[60ch] flex-col gap-4 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          Tradesmen keep the water running, the lights on, and the roofs over our heads. For a
          family of limited means, a small independent tradesman is often the last one willing to
          answer the call.
        </p>
        <p>
          Yet the men who carry others often carry their own burdens alone. Many run one-man shops
          with no employer health plan, no safety net, and no one to call when work slows or a
          crisis hits.
        </p>
        <p>
          We have seen what a brotherhood can do. When one member's family faced a medical emergency
          in his slowest month, fellow Catholics covered the bills within two weeks. The Guild
          exists to make that kind of help ordinary: fair work, faithful friendship, and a community
          rooted in Christ.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-6 lg:sticky lg:top-8 lg:self-start">
      <dl class="border-t border-mortar">
        {facts.map((f) => (
          <div class="grid gap-1 border-b border-mortar py-4 sm:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(0,2fr)] sm:gap-8">
            <dt class="font-sans font-semibold">{f.term}</dt>
            <dd>{f.text}</dd>
          </div>
        ))}
      </dl>
      <p class="font-sans text-[0.85rem] leading-snug text-ash">
        Source: U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics, Census of Fatal Occupational Injuries, 2024.
        Membership figures are the Guild's own.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Section>
